I think this should work:
new.data = expand.grid(lure = seq(min(STQ_um$lure), max(STQ_um$lure), length.out = 50),
                                       habitat = levels(STQ_um$habitat))

This should give you a range of 50 lure values, from the min to max based on your data, for each habitat type. You can change the number of lure values, or any other parameters as per how you want to predict.

best wishes,
Divya

