MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

Ken Kellner can answer best, but I think the interpretation of, say
[moose:grizzly] (Intercept)    0.557

is not that there is a positive interaction between the two, but is just an estimate of the proportion of sites occupied by moose and grizzly on the link scale--the p value here is not really meaningful unless interested in whether the intercept (on the link scale) = 0. So maybe more sites are occupied by moose and predator than by moose alone, or predator alone, or in example 3, more sites are occupied by coyote and wolf than by coyote only or wolf only.

John

