I am getting some instances where adding covariates to each single-species portion of the model (but intercept-only in the interaction) lowers that AIC from a null model causes the interaction term to become non-significant when it was significant in the null model. Is this indicating that the habitat covariates are more important predictors of each species' occupancy than the presence/absence of the other species?

